;; db: bench_bowtie
;; CROSS-RULE REDUNDANCY, factored: the same three queries as
;; bowtie_multi_mono.slog sharing ONE materialized tri/3.  The triangle
;; scan (and its wedge-hub tax) is paid once; each query becomes a cheap
;; join over tri.  Logically identical outputs.
table (edge int int)
table (tri int int int)
table (bt int int int int int)
table (trip int int int int)
table (bb int int int int int int)

rule (edge A B) (edge B C) (edge A C) --> (tri A B C)
rule (tri X Y M) (tri M U V) --> (bt X Y M U V)
rule (tri X Y M) (edge M W) --> (trip X Y M W)
rule (tri X Y M1) (edge M1 M2) (tri M2 U V) --> (bb X Y M1 M2 U V)
